        Personal BaaS demonstrates a security architecture consistent with modern, production-grade
        backend-as-a-service platforms: cryptographically sound authentication, genuine multi-tenant
        isolation at the database layer, and a process-isolated execution model for untrusted code.
        The one critical and one high-severity issue identified in this assessment have already been
        remediated and independently re-verified. The two scheduled medium-severity items are
        well-understood, narrowly scoped, and carry low risk of exploitation in the interim. The
        remaining recommendations are hardening measures, not active exposures.
      </p>
